WEBVTT

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.860
What? You're going home already?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.290
The night's just begun.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.110
I'm not letting you go until morning.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.740
I'm glad to hear that,

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.860
but as they say, you have 
to save the best for last.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.280
I'm delighted to be at 
your service this evening.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.570
I promise I'll make this up to you.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.880
Next time, we'll go until 
noon, not just morning.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.220
It was nice to finally 
hear from you again.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.010
Shame that it was only for this, though.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.410
Thanks.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.810
Are you sure you don't have 
any intention of coming home?

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.470
I don't.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.780
Because my family is here now.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.460
How pretty.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.590
I'm glad you like it.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.370
This smells like caraway.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.850
What kind of medicine is this?

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.780
It's a secret.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.650
You're weird, Luca.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.450
<i>Milady,</i>

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.880
<i>please always stay just as you are...</i>

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.400
<i>my own beloved Lady.</i>

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>But...</i>

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.930
<i>the reason I wish for that is...</i>

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.360
Hey, Princess.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.820
There's a letter from Mama...

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.570
Huh?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.530
Milady? I haven't seen 
her since this morning.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.490
She should have the day off today.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.250
Milady mentioned this morning

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.520
that she was going somewhere with Luca.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.670
Do you know where they went?

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.080
No idea. She didn't say.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.130
Milady?

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.670
She apparently went somewhere 
with Luca this morning.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.760
Do you have any idea 
where they went, Martha?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.950
I haven't heard anything.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.520
What did you need with Milady?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.730
Mama asked us to deliver 
this to Fel in person.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.610
The both of you?

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.080
I wouldn't be with this chickpea 
if that weren't the case—

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.490
Don't call me a chickpea!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.450
My, you two get along so well.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.570
No, we don't!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.260
Oh, by the way, when you see Luca,

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.700
can you ask him to pick up some caraway?

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:50.840
The herb?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:56.330
Yeah. Someone used up all of the stock.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.900
Goodness, you'd think they were 
trying to make a love potion.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.690
Love potion?

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:02.440
Let's go.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.760
Huh? Oh, right.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.390
Don't you think Mama is 
being a little excessive?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.400
"Make sure you both deliver this 
to her in person," she says.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.550
It's because she couldn't count 
on you to do it alone.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.350
You're saying I'm <i>that</i> unreliable?

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.530
Who knows.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.070
At this hour...

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.030
Pace?

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.210
Actually, I haven't seen him yet today.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.940
Well, that failed.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.630
Sorry to have bothered you.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.640
Oh, um...

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.550
Before you leave...

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:47.010
Why is it our responsibility 
to pay Pace's tab, exactly?

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:51.210
We can't ignore it since 
he's part of the family.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.270
The only other person who might know

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.980
where Princess and Luca are...

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.480
Oh, Debito.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.770
Hold it!

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.340
What happened?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.120
That girl cheated at the casino.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.070
All right, leave it to us!

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.540
Wait!

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.660
And who's stupid enough to 
wait when someone says th—

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.770
No one, huh?

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.880
Thanks. You guys are life-savers.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.600
If I'd botched things in the 
capo's absence, he'd be furious.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.380
You mean Debito?

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.500
Yes.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.680
No wonder...

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.850
that was so easy.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.100
What?!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.190
Ciao!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.400
Hey! What do you mean cia—

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.390
W-Wait!

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.790
Damn it. Talk about hard to walk.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:01.550
At this rate, we won't be able 
to split up and look for her.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.830
How inefficient.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.290
We've got no choice.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.970
But we did check all the 
obvious places, right?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.530
Oh? Where are you two 
headed, holding hands?

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.960
Are those the Coin's handcuffs?

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.440
How troublesome.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.400
You won't be able to get those 
off without Debito's keys.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.160
We know.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.030
What are you doing here?

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.660
Is there some kind of law saying

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.910
I'm not allowed to walk 
around during the day?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.380
Well, no...

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.790
I'm shopping.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:36.200
It would appear that someone has used up

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.300
the stock of caraway I need 
to make some medicines.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.330
Caraway?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.960
Hey, is it true that you can 
make a love potion from that?

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.210
Are you planning on making some 
and having Milady drink it?

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.350
N-No!

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.440
I was just curious...

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.070
It must be Luca.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.510
Luca?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:59.790
He'd be able to make one 
that's rather potent.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.210
I see.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.820
So that's why the caraway is all gone.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.540
We're going to go find Princess!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.030
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.450
Enjoy it while you can.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.950
Libertá, calm down.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.800
Don't let Jolly's words get to you.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.740
That would be your weakness.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.130
You think about things too 
much, instead of acting.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.920
It's better than leaping into things head-first!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.510
Aren't you worried about Princess?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.410
Of course I'm worried!

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.020
But running around blindly doesn't help.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.850
We need to find some clues first.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.820
Clues?

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.840
You seem troubled.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.980
You are looking for a girl with red hair.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.690
Are you not?

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.530
There is only one path 
to find what you seek.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.700
Look for the golden-haired 
Athena that brings glory

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.120
to the flowers of Regalo.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.590
The goddess' white ball of yarn

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:05.500
will be what leads you down 
the path you cannot see.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.020
What the hell does that mean?

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.440
It's a simple riddle.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.220
"The flowers of Regalo"

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.280
refers to the women of this island.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.010
The one who brings them glory...

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.500
Not to mention, Athena is 
the goddess of weaving.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.500
Regalo's golden-haired 
goddess of weaving is...

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:28.440
Oh?

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.270
Did something good happen?

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:36.310
Mondo.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:38.610
Why don't you try and guess?

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.530
Felicitá happened to say,

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.870
"Papa, I love you!" in her sleep, 
or something like that?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.140
You're such the doting father.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.710
She'll dislike you even more.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.540
Actually...

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.070
That's perfect.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.990
My wife is quite the schemer.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.560
I just want them to get along.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.560
I am, after all, like their mother.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.700
Jeez. First Dante, now you...

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.230
We have quite a group...

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.050
Libertá and Nova are 
both doing their best

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.470
to overcome themselves.

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.250
By spending time with each other,

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.190
I'm hoping they will come to 
understand each other's differences

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.350
and learn to respect each other.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:28.000
Then both of their Arcana powers 
should become stronger.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.410
To be honest,

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.740
I wanted them to be 
able to relax a little.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.450
You're right.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.980
Time is limited.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.930
I'm a happy man.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.580
I have the best wife, the best daughter,

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:45.810
and the best family.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.030
I have more than what most people 
can obtain in a lifetime.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.980
So, my Madame Butterfly,

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:58.270
please don't look like that.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.520
All right, everyone.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.000
We're almost there.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.710
I think this every year, but...

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.380
this is too far away!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.560
No kidding.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:17.300
I know it's so we can do this 
behind Jolly's back, but...

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:19.180
Behind Jolly's back?

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.720
Indeed.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.530
You are aware that I

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:26.370
am growing herbs for alchemy 
in the yard, correct?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.180
Yes.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:31.000
That terrible person uses 
them without permission.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.360
In huge quantities, at that.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.320
Well, he believes, 
"what's yours is mine."

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.660
So, I made a small herb garden

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.060
out here where he can't find it.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:43.660
You could call it Luca's secret base.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.350
And we're dragged along once a year

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.120
to help harvest the herbs.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.420
I had no idea...

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.610
Milady,

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:57.510
even I have a secret or two.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.220
Luca, let's take a break.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:05.580
I'm so hungry that I 
have no strength left.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.860
Didn't you bring a bit too much?

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:11.440
Well, before lunch, 
there's the morning snack,

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.920
the noon snack, and then 
the 3 o'clock snack.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.660
That's all food?!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.030
Yes. And this year, 
there's one more thing...

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:19.310
What?

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.110
It's a secret.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.070
And with that...

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.080
Ta-da!

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:29.460
The morning snack is cannoli 
stuffed with ricotta cheese.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:31.820
How is it?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:33.460
I bought them from the 
best shop in Regalo.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.520
Yes, it's deli—

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:37.680
Delicious, right?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.200
Pace.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.890
Huh? Did I do something wrong?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.150
Even I've never done anything 
like that to Milady.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.450
Why, exactly, do the two of us 
have to follow some cat around?

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.610
I'm not very fond of the idea either.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:14.040
So the golden-haired 
goddess was Ms. Federica,

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.710
and I even get that the white 
ball of yarn was the cat.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.670
But it's not exactly a dog.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.030
Since it's supposed to lead us 
down a path we cannot see,

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:24.490
we've no other choice.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:29.850
Pace!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.480
Well done. Very brave.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:41.050
But, Bambina, you needn't worry.

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.950
All the traps here are made by Luca.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.320
They are?

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.590
They're to keep Jolly away.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:51.260
Pace, you fell for this 
exact trap last year.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:53.210
You need to remember already.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:54.800
Not possible.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.980
This birdbrain will forget everything 
after taking three steps.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.490
Could you say something 
in my defense, Princess?

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.920
Isn't this going a bit far, Luca?

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:04.710
It's fine.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.110
Actually, this wouldn't 
be enough for Jolly.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:10.310
Do you not like Jolly?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.770
He's your teacher in alchemy, right?

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.090
Indeed.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:17.560
That man is a genius alchemist.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.830
But I cannot admire him.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.740
Please keep your distance 
from him, Milady.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.990
Luca...

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:35.620
I think I'm hungry again.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.650
Let's hurry to the herb garden 
so we can have some lunch.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.350
No kidding.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.610
Let's hurry up and get out 
of this annoying place.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:45.760
Debito, not there!

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.050
Oops.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.080
Why is it always me?!

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.560
Goodness, you two.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.350
Come on now, we're almost there.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:02.440
Please mind the traps by your feet.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.320
So tired.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.280
Someone let me down!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.700
All the way out here?

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.200
Damn, it's no use.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.200
What are you doing?

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.070
I was just seeing if I could get

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.900
this out with my left hand somehow.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.630
But I guess I can't.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.710
How stupid.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.350
We may need it.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.800
I have a really bad feeling.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.810
Indeed, it's best to be on our guard.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.560
But if something happens, 
I'll fight with this.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.990
We don't need your sword.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.900
Not needed, huh?

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.380
Let's go.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.360
Yeah.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.700
Yeah! Lunchtime!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:56.480
Here.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:57.470
Huh?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.870
If any will not work, neither let him eat.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.650
All right, everyone!

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.540
It's time for super happy 
fun harvesting times!

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.710
You're so excited.

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:08.720
There's a certain herb that I'd 
like to harvest before lunch.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.640
Pace, please go over there.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.640
Debito, over there, please.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.970
What can I do to help?

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.850
Oh, Milady.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.610
If you would just stand 
right there, Milady.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:22.380
You've gotta be kidding!

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.860
Your fever for Milady 
has finally gone critical.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.940
I'll help, too.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.860
So let's hurry up and finish 
so we can have lunch.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.200
Yes, Milady!

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:43.000
Debito! What kind of method is that?!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.860
And I'm spent.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:48.090
Is it time for lunch yet, Luca?

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.960
Please hold out a little longer.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.550
According to my calculations, 
we should be almost done.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.170
Are you sure it's going to be all right?

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:57.310
Is something going on?

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.180
It's still a secret, Milady.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.570
<i>My best work.</i>

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:08.880
<i>I'm anxious to see the results.</i>

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:14.120
Well, it's a good thing you're short.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:15.160
Hey!

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:19.320
Damn it! Move your leg, it's in the way!

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.120
Yeah, yeah, almighty Nova.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.090
If it was Luca who set 
such elaborate traps...

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.270
It means he's pretty serious.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:34.760
Wait!

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.060
I'm borrowing this!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.230
Ooh! Giapponese swords aren't bad.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:47.650
Libertá, you...

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:55.600
Nova...

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:00.810
Let's go!

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:01.410
Yeah.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.250
Princess!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:05.000
Felicitá!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:05.960
Huh?

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:06.930
Huh?

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.490
Hey, you're late.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:10.550
Thanks for your hard work!

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:16.990
What was that scream?

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:20.160
Oh, there was a bug in her apple.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.020
Thank you for your hard work.

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:26.960
It appears the potion worked quite well.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.190
That's right! The potion!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.350
This is a potion that 
Mama asked me to make.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:33.280
It's only effective on cats.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:36.240
I left a trail with it leading to us.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:38.300
Mama asked you?

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:39.050
Indeed.

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.100
Come to think of it, 
we were trying to deliver

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.530
Mama's letter to Princess...

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.710
What do you mean?

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:49.010
In short, this was all a surprise from Mama

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.340
for Bambina and the two little kids.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.920
Or, you could say you 
fell for her scheme.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.430
Exactly.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.140
All of us naughty adults 
were Mama's accomplices.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.530
Did you have fun?

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.360
It wasn't bad.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.230
We're finally free!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.650
Sorry about earlier.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:22.160
For using your sword without asking.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:26.350
That was an emergency,

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:27.830
and I used your sword, as well.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.110
There's no need to apologize.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:38.100
Hey, Princess. What did Mama say?

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.000
Fel?

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.020
Oh?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.320
It looks like something 
good happened, Miss Sumire.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.110
All thanks to your wonderful 
acting, Ms. Jovanna.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.660
All right, line up!

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:05.080
Debito, don't look so scary!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.610
That was your secret luggage?

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.940
Yeah. This was the first time

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.680
that someone other than the three 
of us came to this secret base.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:15.300
So I wanted to have a record 
of this momentous occasion.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.250
Come on, smile!

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:20.180
It's a fun souvenir photograph!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:22.390
All right, here we go!

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:27.430
Un, due, tre! Lasagna!

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.970
<i>Luca and Debito haven't 
changed at all, have they?</i>

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.350
<i>Don't worry, Mom.</i>

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:42.020
<i>We're all pretty happy.</i>

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.540
"A record of this momentous occasion"?

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:50.560
You've got to be kidding, Pace.

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.070
They all look great.

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.350
I've got to start distancing 
myself from Milady soon...

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:06.850
Indeed.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.780
Children grow into adults 
before you know it.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:19.040
I went to Luca's herb garden 
with Libertá today.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:20.760
It was rough.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:24.220
But it was fun.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:30.180
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.280
<i>I'll become stronger so I can...</i>

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.420
Oh, Mama...

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.380
<i>To my precious daughter:</i>

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.530
<i>Please reward these brave 
young men with a kiss.</i>

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.190
<i>On the cheek, of course.</i>

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:46.420
<i>Love, Mama.</i>

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.400
Gli Amanti...

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:38.000
We will now begin our 
repentance for the day.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:41.250
Choose the one who should be 
punished, by naming their card.

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:42.520
La Forza.

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:43.920
La Temperanza.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.260
Tonight's sinner is you, La Forza!

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:48.320
What?!

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:49.590
Why me?

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:53.160
I thought I was going to 
be able to take a picture

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:55.240
with only Milady...

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:59.600
What do you mean we could 
only take one picture?!

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:03.900
Apparently, those plates break easily.

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:05.990
I had no idea.

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:07.900
So...

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:10.360
Let's eat!

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:13.620
Buono!

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:13.450
Buono!

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.330
This is irresistible.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.870
What a shame for those who can't eat it.

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:21.400
I want to eat... lasagna...

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:22.710
Lasagna!

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.760
Lasagna!

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:33.380
Apparently, the next 
episode will be

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:34.500
me killing that old man.

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:36.940
What? It's not a story about 
all-you-can-eat lasagna?

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:39.420
No, next time will be me and Milady's...

00:23:39.760 --> 00:23:40.980
This guy's scary...
